  "query_preview": "..\n\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Gusty winds on Saturday creating choppy conditions for area\n  lakes, especially across northwest Montana.\n\n- Cooler and showery by early to mid next week.\n\nHigh pressure remains in place over western Montana and north\ncentral Idaho today resulting in warm conditions above normal for\nthis time of year. Patchy valley fog is possible again this\nmorning but should dissipate by this afternoon.\n\nA dry cold front is still expected to move through the region on\nSaturday. Breezy conditions will develop area wide, though the\nstrongest winds are anticipated across northwest Montana. West\nwinds gusting 30 to 40 mph are anticipated, which will create\nchoppy conditions on area lakes, including Flathead Lake. The\nincreased wind will allow for better atmospheric mixing, allowing\ntemperatures to top out into the upper 60s to near 70 for many\nvalley locations.  \n\nTemperatures will trend cooler behind the front on Sunday, though\nstill running a few degrees warmer than normal. Brief high\npressure will build back over the region early next week,\nmaintaining coll mornings and warm afternoons through Tuesday.  \n\nForecast models continue to cut off a large area of low pressure\nalong the west coast by mid next week. With most of the energy\nwith this system digging well south, it appears the Northern\nRockies will be under split flow aloft. This will result in\ncooler temperatures and unsettled (showery) conditions.",
